# Fixture — the 2026-10-17 dispatcher-wedge false-restart incident (card
# t_160d306f). Seeded from the real ~/.hermes/logs/gateway.log (lines
# ~22401-22524); personal data redacted (home paths -> /Users/<operator>,
# chat ids -> <redacted>), timestamps kept verbatim (local time).
#
# What happened: card t_4e0f0509 on a foreign board sat READY but was held
# by the dispatcher's OWN respawn guard (an open PR -> active_pr=1). The
# dispatcher correctly refused to respawn and said so in every stuck warning
# ("Last tick held back: active_pr=1."). The hscc dispatcher-wedge watchdog
# read the red warning anyway and kicked `launchctl kickstart` for the
# gateway at 12:13, 12:43 and 13:17 — three restarts in ~65 minutes for a
# dispatcher that was working exactly as designed.
